---
import Pane from '../Pane.astro'
---
<section class="act" data-act="2" aria-labelledby="act2-heading">
  <div class="copy">
    <h2 id="act2-heading">The envelope teaches the peer how to answer</h2>
    <p>
      One <code>channel_send</code> later, the peer's pane holds this —
      visible plaintext, by design: human observability is a feature. It
      carries a correlation id and the exact command the peer needs to reply
      with.
    </p>
    <p>
      Always exactly one line: an envelope carries no control characters, so
      tmux can inject it into any pane safely.
    </p>
  </div>
  <Pane title="tmux:%3 — codex" active={true}>
    <pre tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="tmux pane contents: an uplink envelope with the reply command"><code
      data-typewriter
      data-text={"[uplink from:claude pane:%1 id:6b3b20e6] review my diff (reply: run `tmux send-keys -t %1 -l '[reply id:6b3b20e6] <your answer>' \\; send-keys -t %1 Enter`)"}
    >[uplink from:claude pane:%1 id:6b3b20e6] review my diff (reply: run `tmux send-keys -t %1 -l '[reply id:6b3b20e6] &lt;your answer&gt;' \; send-keys -t %1 Enter`)</code></pre>
    <span class="signal" data-signal aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </Pane>
</section>

<style>
  .act {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-l);
    padding: var(--space-xl) var(--space-m);
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    align-items: center;
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) { .act { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.2fr; } }
  /* See Act0.astro for why grid items need this: an unbreakable line in the
     pane's <pre> would otherwise force the shared grid column past the
     viewport, even though the <pre> itself scrolls. `trap`/`tip` text in the
     sibling acts comes from the marketplace entry, not this repo, so this is
     defensive against future copy, not just today's. */
  .copy { min-width: 0; }
  h2 { font-size: var(--step-2); line-height: 1.1; margin: 0 0 var(--space-m); }
  .copy p { color: var(--fg-dim); max-width: 44ch; }
  pre { margin: 0; overflow-x: auto; }
  .signal {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    width: 2px;
    height: 100%;
    /* The signal is the one place the brand's warm amber appears in the page
       body: the message crossing the cold field. Palette decision 2026-07-29. */
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, transparent, var(--signal), transparent);
    opacity: 0;
    will-change: transform, opacity;
  }
</style>
